@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "zendesk.integration"

Feature: OSB to Zendesk Partner and Customer Ticket Integration
	Testing ticket changes when a project has partners and customers on it.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
	* I generate a provisioning project name
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.customer2                       |
	| Email Address | osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer2                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.partner1                      |
	| Email Address | osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                               |
	| Last Name     | Partner1                          |
	* I generate static start and end dates
	* I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Name   | Osbpar - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Code   | OSBPAROSBPAR                  | |
	| Status | Active                        | |
	* I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Osbpar - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Service Partnership" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Partner"
	* I assign the contact with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" on the account "Osbpar - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Partner Member |
	* I create an assigned team nested field for a team with the name "Osbpar - ${staticProjectName}" assigned to the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	* I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Assigned Team Nested Field | ${staticAssignedTeamNestedField} | |
	| Code                       | OSBZENOSBZEN                     | |
	| Language                   | English                          | |
	| Name                       | Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}    | |
	| Region                     | United States                    | |
	| Status                     | Active                           | |
	| Tier                       | T1                               | |
	* I assign the team with the name "Osbpar - ${staticProjectName}" on the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Partner |
	* I assign the team with the name "Osbpar - ${staticProjectName}" on the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| First Line Support |
	* I create a postal address for an account with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" on koroneiki with the following values
	| Country               | United States   |
	| Locality              | Diamond Bar     |
	| Region                | California      |
	| Type                  | Business        |
	| Mailing               | True            |
	| Postal Code           | 91765           |
	| Primary               | True            |
	| Street Address Line 1 | 123 Main Street |

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Osbpar - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I teardown the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Osbpar - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Osbzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| OSBPAROSBPAR |
	| OSBZENOSBZEN |
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| OSBPAROSBPAR |
	| OSBZENOSBZEN |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| New Subscription(s) for Osbpar - ${staticProjectName} |
	| New Subscription(s) for Osbzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Osbpar - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Osbzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View partner removal with open ticket when customers are remaining
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	Last partners with open tickets should not be removed when customers are remaining.

	Given I assign the contact with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Requester |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Requester |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Portal Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 6 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Gold Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the support organization with the code "OSBZENOSBZEN" should be part of the support site
	And the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	When I wait for "60" seconds
	And I create a request as a user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product           | prd_liferay_portal_6_2                           |
	| Component         | activation_key_project_administration            |
	| System Status     | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject           | Request Subject                                  |
	| Description       | Request Description                              |
	| Organization Name | Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}                    |
	Then the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the status "new"
	And the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the requester with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken"
	When I wait for "60" seconds
	And I remove customer contacts with the following email addresses from the account "Osbpar - ${staticProjectName}"
	| osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	Then the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the default user from the organization with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" as the requester

Scenario: View customer removal with open ticket when partner is remaining
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	Last customers with open tickets should not be removed when partners are remaining.

	Given I assign the contact with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Requester |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
